From 4b392175428965e1c1d71b1634fcac0a5341195f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:38:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 94/97] XHTTP: Let no data past a stream's shown upload window
 reach the handler

The governor reset a stream whose client sent past the window it was
shown, but forwarded the offending DATA frame to its stack first; the
stack, given a larger window, took it into the request body, and with
END_STREAM the handler read past the window and saw the body end
cleanly before the reset came. Stock rejects the frame before any of it
reaches the body. The frame is now dropped, and its bytes count as
returned on the connection, as a stack returns connection credit for
data it refused.

TestFlowUploadPastWindowAsStock compares the handler's body with a stock
server's, with and without END_STREAM; TestFlowClientPastShownWindow
also checks that nothing of the frame reaches the stack and that the
connection counts it returned.

An empty frame takes no window and is past none: a server that lowered
its window can leave a stream past it before an empty frame with
END_STREAM comes, and that frame passes on as before
(TestFlowModelProtocol). The handler test waits for the connection
window it sends into, where it waited a fixed 200 ms and now and then
sent past the connection's window instead of the stream's.
